## Real-World Attack Scenario

1. Target: secure-bank.com (well-protected)
2. Reverse IP reveals: old-blog.com on same server
3. old-blog.com runs WordPress 4.0 (vulnerable)
4. Attacker exploits old-blog.com
5. Gains server access → Pivots to secure-bank.com

## Prevention Measures

1. **Use VPS or Dedicated Hosting** - Isolate critical applications
2. **Implement Container Isolation** - Docker/Kubernetes separation
3. **Regular Audits** - Monitor all co-hosted sites
4. **Keep Everything Updated** - CMS, plugins, server software
5. **Know Your Neighbors** - Research who shares your server

## Key Takeaway

> Shared hosting means shared risk. Your security is only as strong as your weakest co-hosted neighbor.

